    "narrative": "With limited action on the slate, the focus for the Austin Waves today centers on the marginal utility of **Brayan Rocchio**. Currently slotted at 40.89, **Brayan Rocchio** occupies the absolute basement of our starting criteria. While his base projection remains steady, the combination of a bottom-of-the-order assignment (#9) and a neutral matchup against Peralta creates a low ceiling. We are deploying **Brayan Rocchio** purely to maintain volume, but he remains a high-risk play that sits just barely above our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold; any late lineup adjustment shifting him further down the order could necessitate an immediate pivot to avoid wasting a game cap on a sub-optimal outing.\n\nThe bench decision process was straightforward today, largely dictated by the combination of team off-days for core producers like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker**, and the ongoing IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, who remains unavailable for selection. The most notable omission remains **Liam Hicks**, who fell short of our efficiency floor with a 29.95 score. Despite a relatively workable matchup against Messick, the combination of a negative park factor and a platoon disadvantage against a left-handed arm suppressed his value significantly. Without an elite platoon edge to leverage, **Liam Hicks** does not offer the necessary floor to warrant a start in a 5x5 Roto format where efficiency is paramount. We will proceed with caution, relying on **Brayan Rocchio** as our lone active representative while awaiting the return of our primary catalysts to anchor the lineup in future sessions.",
